cat VIEW THE FILE AND WORK WITH FILE CONTENT

>cat is used to display, combine and create a file content in linux

1. View the file Content 

   syntax : cat filename

   Example : cat index.html


2.Show line numbers

  syntax : cat -n filename

  Example : cat -n demo.txt

3. View the Multiple Files Contents One After Other

  syntax : cat file1 file2

  Example : cat configure.txt file2.txt

4.Create a file using cat
 
  syntax : cat > filename

  Example : cat > devops.txt

  if file already exist this command will overwrite the exist content

  press Ctrl + D for save and exit

5. Add new content to the end of the existing file using cat, without deleting the old content

  syntax : cat >> filename

  Example : cat >> devops.txt

  press Ctrl + D for save and exit

6. Combine the multiple file contents into one new file

  syntax : cat file1 file2 > output.txt

  Example : cat devops.txt SELinux-demo.html > combinefile.txt

