sed -->Stream Editor

1. sed command is used to search , replace, delete, or print a text with out enter a editor

>s is sed stands for substitute and it is used for replace the old text with new text

Syntax : sed 'operation' filename

Example : sed 's/Linux/DevOps' testfile.txt

s --> substitue/replace
Linux --> old text
DevOps --> new text

2. sed -i permanent replcement inside the file

 Syntax : sed -i 's/old/new' filename

 Example : sed -i 's/DevOps/Linux' testfile.txt

 the file is permanently modify , we use sed without i after modify peramently sed only change the file temporarly original file cannot modify

3. global replacement (g) : it replcaes the matches occuerances in each line ,not just first one

  Syntax : sed 's/old/new/g' filename

  Example : 
  > cat >> tools.txt
 
  Docker Docker Jenkins
  Linux Docker Docker

  Ctrl + D

  command : sed 's/Docker/Kubernetes/g' tools.txt

  > cat tools.txt 

  Kubernetes Kubernetes Jenkins
  Linux Kubernetes Kubernetes

  we want to chanage permanently use "sed -i" 

4. Deleting Lines : sed 'Nd' --> Delete a specific lines
 
   N -> Number of Lines
   d -> Delete

   Syntax : sed 'Nd' filename

   Example : sed '2d' testfile.txt -->delete lines from the output

   we want use to delete permanently sed -i 

   Example : sed -i '2d' testfile.txt --> delete lines permanently from the file

5.sed -n --> print specific lines

 sed -n is used to show only the specific lines 

 Syntax : sed -n 'Np' filename

  N = number of lines
  p = print
  -n = normal output

  Example: sed -n '5p' textfile.txt

  if we want to print mulptiple lines

  Example : sed -n '2,5p' textfile.txt

  it prints the line 2 through 5

6. sed -n '/word/p' -->print the matching lines

   Syntax : sed -n '/word/p' filename

   Example : sed -n '/jenkins/p' jenkins.sh
