File Permissions 
=====================================================================================================
1. chmod ---> Change permissions

chmod is used to change the file and directories permissions

4 = read(r)
2 = write(w)
1 = excute(x)

add them together

7 : 4 + 2 + 1 = rwx
6 : 4 + 2     = r-w
5 : 4+1       = r-x
4 : 4         = r--
3 : 2 + 1     = -wx
2 : 2         = -w-
1 : 1         = --x
0 : 0         = ---

Example = chmod 755 testfile.txt

it gives read, write, execute to the owner and read, execute to group and others.


2. chown -->change file owner

chown is used to change the owner of a file or directory

Syntax : chown username filename

Example : chown server testfile.txt

> change owner and group 

  chown username:groupname filename

  Example : chown server:devops testfile.txt


3. chgrp --> change group only

chgrp is used to change the group of a file or directory.

Syntax : chgrp groupname filename

